[[0,1041871,0,2,0,2,"2016-05-15T08:59:47","luckyguy","[e]",[],"<p>I'm trying to install openvz in arch to mirror some vps's I have. Openvz can't be found in the packages, in the AUR. Earlier today I installed a SUSE exclusive package to arch from the AUR. Arch has everything. Does anybody have any insight on why Arch is having such a hard time with openvz?</p>","Is there a reason arch refuses to support openvz","","arch"],[1,5200714,0,0,0,0,"2016-05-15T09:21:25","luckyguy","[e]",[],"<p>Edit: Let's see if compiling this source that took forever to find is more than I can chew.</p>\n<p>First step:</p>\n<pre><code>parallel git clone https;//src.openvz.org/scm/ovz/{}.git\ncriu\nlibprlcommon\nlibprlsdk\nlibprlxmlmodel\nlibreport-plugin-virtuozzo\nlibvcmmd\nlibvzctl\nlibvzevent\nlibvzsock\nopenvz-mirrors\nopenvz-planet\np.haul\npcompact\nploop\nprl-disk-tool\nprl-disp-service\nprl-vzvncserver\nprlctl\nprl_nettool\nrmond\nrmond-drs\nvcmmd\nvz-docs\nvz-meta\nvzctl\nvzkernel\nvzmigrate\nvzstat\nvztt\n[Ctrl-d]\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Maybe I can parallel my whole way throught it ;)</p>"]]
